From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: qualcomm: iceland: A power-on boot menu on the keys

The Pad 4 is to start Fedora or, once the disk is split, LineageOS. ABL
starts boot_b (U-Boot) in both cases; LineageOS's kernel goes into
recovery_b, which ABL starts in recovery mode. The choice is a U-Boot
bootmenu on the tablet's keys: Volume Up / Volume Down move, Power
selects (button-kbd with the phone key remapping, already in the
config). 5 s, then the default, Fedora.

- mach-snapdragon: qcom_keys_released <s>: wait until no button is held
  (200 ms), then drop the console's queue. button-kbd makes a character
  when a key is released, so the power-on press would select an entry.
  A key still held after <s>: the command fails, no menu.
- mach-snapdragon: qcom_recovery_gate [if]: read only. Succeeds only when
  exactly one disk has "userdata", the same disk has "fedora" (userdata
  is Android's), and recovery_b starts with a boot image header v3 / v4
  whose kernel is an arm64 Image. Until then no LineageOS entry exists,
  so it is never offered while userdata holds Fedora.
- mach-snapdragon: qcom_reboot_mode <recovery|bootloader>: store the
  DT's mode-recovery / mode-bootloader in the nvmem-reboot-mode cell
  (fastboot.c's store: read, modify, write, read back), then reset. If
  the store fails, nothing is reset.
- env: the menu runs after the disk is mapped. Entries: Fedora (leave
  the menu), LineageOS (only when the gate is open), Boot loader
  (fastboot). Not on a charger start (ABL boot mode "charger", patch
  0011): Fedora at once, its charging target takes over, and no key can
  start another OS. Every new line is install-only: the rehearsal env
  is unchanged.
- No U-Boot console: bootmenu runs only inside bootcmd, so its own
  "Exit" line (and ESC) returns there and the boot goes on to Fedora,
  like the timeout. BOOTMENU_DISABLE_UBOOT_CONSOLE is not set: it needs
  AUTOBOOT_MENU_SHOW, which would run an EFI boot menu before bootcmd.

U-Boot resets only for an entry the owner picked with Power, after the
reboot reason was stored and read back. Volume Down at power-on still
reaches ABL's fastboot before U-Boot runs.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
